SCOPE OF THE PROJECT'S LICENCE

The maintainer's original code, documentation, directory descriptions and site
content are licensed under CC BY 4.0. The grant also covers any copyright and
sui generis database rights the maintainer holds in the selection and arrangement
of the directory. It applies only to rights the maintainer can grant, not to
every element of a data file, generated page or repository checkout.

You may share and adapt the licensed material, including commercially, subject
to the full licence terms. Give appropriate credit, link to the licence and
indicate changes; retain supplied notices as required by the licence. Do not
suggest endorsement. No additional restrictions are imposed on licensed uses.
This notice summarises the scope; it does not modify the CC BY 4.0 legal code.

Suggested citation:
  Cano Trigueros, J. A. (2026). FarmSuccession: farm succession, access to land,
  aid and training in Europe. https://farmsuccession.eu/

THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL AND PERMISSIONS

Third-party texts, quotations (including sources[].quotes entries in
JSON editions and research briefs), photographs, logos, documents, databases,
linked pages and the preserved historical toolkit are not relicensed by this
grant. Their own licences, rights and conditions apply. Source URLs and reading
dates identify evidence; they do not constitute reuse authorisation.

FarmSuccession has contacted some organisations for specific permissions. This
is not a claim that every source has granted permission or endorses the project.
A permission specifically given to FarmSuccession does not automatically extend
to reusers. Check the original terms and, where authorisation is needed, contact
the rights holder or responsible organisation directly. FarmSuccession cannot
grant rights on their behalf.

Ordinary links, mentions, unprotected facts and uses permitted by an applicable
licence or law do not always require separate permission. This notice does not
restrict lawful uses or require attribution merely for linking. Any applicable
third-party database rights must also be assessed for the intended reuse.

CODE AND DEPENDENCIES

The project's own code remains under its existing CC BY 4.0 licence; this change
clarifies scope and does not adopt a different software licence. Third-party
software, fonts and icons retain their respective licences, including when
bundled in the generated site. See frontend/public/licenses/ for the notices
for the shipped fonts, Lucide icons and Pagefind search assets; installed
packages carry additional dependency and build-tool notices. A package.json
licence field describes the project's own work, not all of its dependencies.

